Lorena Iniguez is the only female performer in Sones de Mexico Ensemble, a Mexican folk group that shares music and dance from all different parts of Mexico. An immigrant of Mexican parents, Iniguez says her ancestry and Mexican culture is a vital component to her identity growing up and living her life in Chicago. Navy Pier hosts "Neighborhoods of the World," a series celebrating different cultures in Chicago each Sunday. Iniguez and Sones de Mexico performed at the Pier to celebrate Mexican culture the first Sunday in April.